Sval: mach artifact installs the test GMP plugins where the harnesses load them

Backport of Mozilla's Bug 2064182 (mozilla-central e1685d244084, Firefox
156), unchanged. ESR 153 does not carry it. ArtifactJob.test_artifact_patterns
is a set, and a test GMP plugin's file matches both "bin/plugins/gmp-*/*/*"
(to dist/bin) and "bin/plugins/*" (to dist/plugins). The first match wins, and
a set's order follows string hashing, which Python randomizes in each
process, so which of the two an artifact build used changed from one mach
process to the next, and its processed archive kept the result. The
mochitest harness loads the plugins from dist/bin (mochitest_options.py,
gmp_path), and the GMP process stops with MOZ_CRASH(Plugin file does not
exist) when the library is missing there.
Drop this patch when the upstream pin reaches Firefox 156.

